WEBVTT

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.120
Previously on Enterprise

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.840
Casualty list yet? So far the news isn't good.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.670
Five people are confirmed dead. Dozens wounded.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:21.620
If you destroy Earth, you won't just be eliminating my species, you'll be eliminating your own.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.700
Do you have any idea why they released you?

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.660
I think it may have gotten through to one of them.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.970
We were told the reptilians...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.610
Well, who told you this?

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:38.490
We've also learned that they were building this bioweapon in the past, on Earth.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:45.700
When I was exposed to Trillium, it affected me in a way I wasn't prepared for.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.760
I discovered I was able to access certain emotions.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:50.900
I wanted them.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.320
They devised a way to it, injected into my bloodstream.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.060
You must have known it was dangerous.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.520
Trillium exposure is deadly to Vulcan.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:29.930
More than anyone could ask.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:40.910
to and then some. And so have all of you. I wanted to say thank you. I wish I could thank the 18

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:50.080
crewmen who were lost. Like you, they understood how important our mission is and they accepted

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:57.460
the risks. We came into the expanse not knowing what we'd find. With no one to rely on but

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:59.980
ourselves, we're going to...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:11.990
To accomplish our mission for everyone on earth who's relying on us for the 18

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:38.690
See my dream come and watch the sky

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:43.500
Down no more

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.430
Then I change my mind

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:42.370
We managed to get into section six and seven on C deck, we found Taylor and Kamada.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:44.670
That accounts for everyone.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.180
What's our status on weapons?

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:53.580
Mr. Reed has both forward phase cannons back on line, in addition to the aft torpedo launchers.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:56.170
Hull plating is up to 80%.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.290
That'll have to do.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:58.730
We could wait.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.180
Hang back until we've had a chance to make more repairs.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:03.760
Degra's message was clear.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.680
We're to meet him ten hours from now.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.360
Then I don't intend to be late.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:08.780
Maybe that's what he's counting on.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.680
Lure us into an ambush while we're still licking our wounds.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.580
That'd be my decision.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:15.220
We have a lot of work to do.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.340
I suggest we get to.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:17.710
Aye, sir.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:26.010
Commander, Ruman Taylor was one of yours, wasn't she?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.160
She was an EPS control specialist.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:31.360
Damn good one.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:37.890
I'd like you to write a letter to her family.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:42.620
She worked on Rostov's team.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:43.460
I can ask him.

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:44.380
I asked you.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:47.710
I'm barely holding the ship together.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:49.610
I don't have time to sit down and write a letter.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:50.990
It doesn't have to be long.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.300
I mean, deserves to know what happened to her.

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:12.090
You're busy. I'll come back.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:15.800
Have a seat. I'll have to use a hand scanner.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.100
The imaging chamber is still offline.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:23.050
Commander Tucker reassigned the repair team that was working here.

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:26.050
He said the armory was a higher priority.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.970
You'll see how low a priority I am the next time he burns his fingers.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.220
I think it's on a plasma conduit.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:31.740
Ah.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:33.140
Ah.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:36.160
You've experienced no further withdrawal symptoms?

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:37.280
No.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.460
I'm only detecting trace amounts of trillium in your system.

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:41.960
Hardly worth mentioning.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:47.720
That's good news, is it?

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:57.550
These emotions have grown more difficult to control.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:05:59.980
My usual tech...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.260
for suppressing them haven't been effective.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:10.560
Earth, there is a cautionary tale

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:14.120
about the dangers of releasing a magical creature

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.820
called a genie from a bottle.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:20.420
Once it's out, it's extremely difficult to put back in.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:24.480
Are you saying these emotions may never subside?

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:26.750
You used Trelium for three months.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:29.850
It caused significant damage to your neural.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:34.500
You may have to learn to live with these emotions.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.290
We're approaching the coordinates, Captain.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:41.820
Right on the schedule.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:45.270
Nice ship's out there, son.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:48.840
Pushy.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:50.900
Scanning all frequencies.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:52.800
Nothing so far.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:54.300
Maybe they're running late.

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:57.490
Snow alert.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:06:58.960
It's a spatial anomaly.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:02.650
We've entered a dense field.

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:16.530
Trev, hold some injuries on V-Deck.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:21.810
Sir.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:25.020
Get us out of here.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:25.780
Aye, sir.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:35.760
We're receiving a transmission.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:37.090
Stay cool.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:38.730
He's telling us to follow him.

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:51.030
We're the traps.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:03.610
They're hailing us.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.290
I see you found my message.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.480
We have a great deal to discuss, and I don't have much time.

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:11.990
Come aboard my ship.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.850
If we'd left you with the Reptilians, they would have killed you.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:24.180
Igra arranged for the Aquatics to return you to your ship.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:26.980
And you also called off the attack on Enterprise.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:29.980
The Reptilians weren't very pleased.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:37.050
about that either. You've taken a big risk. If you're telling the truth, the future of my people

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:46.560
is at stake. Everything I've told you is true. Forgive me. Council will need more than your

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:55.360
word. Perhaps you can demonstrate your ability to time travel. That might be a bit difficult.

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:05.920
But if you come aboard my ship, I can give you all the proof you want.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:09.360
Very well.

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:11.640
But there's some things I want to know first.

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:12.920
Such as?

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:15.200
When will your weapon be launched?

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:20.860
Such date hasn't been determined yet.

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:22.680
Weeks? Days?

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:24.140
That's up to the council.

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:25.530
I'm trying to help you.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:28.960
But I need to know my world isn't being destroyed while I'm doing it.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:29.920
The weapon?

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:37.720
won't be launched for several days. Show us your proof we can to stop it.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:07.140
What'd you get?

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:10.750
Pepperoni pizza.

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:14.870
Or you can pick the pepperoni on it.

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:19.290
Damage reports?

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:20.490
No.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:24.460
Captain wants me to write a letter to Freeman Taylor's family.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:26.960
Sure, they'll appreciate that.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:29.870
Your daughter's dead.

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:39.780
really think they'll care what I have to say. When's the last time you slept? I don't know.

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:52.930
Not since the attack. That was two days ago. All right, then. Two days. Go to your quarters.

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:59.970
Get some sleep. Believe me, I'd love to. I could order you. I don't have time.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:04.360
We're full of holes. The only thing keeping us flying is a stolen warp coil.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:06.640
And now you've got to write this letter.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:29.810
Engineering, shut down the auxiliary coolant lines between sections 12 and 14.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:38.680
On either sickbay, medical emergency on EDAC, section 12.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:39.880
On my way, Commander.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:43.680
Reactor pressure's holding.

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:46.650
I think I wasn't taking a nap.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:08.020
Damron, colleague of sorts.

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:11.390
They're the ones we found on Earth in the past.

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:13.980
And this is the result of your finding them?

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:17.900
They were about to release a bioweapon that decimated the population.

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:24.000
Reptilians felt a toxin would be more effective on your species.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:28.150
Damron and his team disappeared shortly after the Council rejected his proposal.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:35.190
decided to go ahead without your counsel's approval but fortunately you

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:40.210
were able to stop them by traveling back through time I already told you we had

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:45.440
help just like they did this proves nothing how do we know he didn't

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:49.370
capture them in the present you need more evidence

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:32.640
I had this with them.

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:37.730
We destroyed the toxin, but my doctor kept a sample of it in stasis.

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:44.480
This appears to be Xindi technology, but I'd like to have our engineers confirm it.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:47.660
Have them come aboard, perform whatever test they'd like.

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:53.000
This proves nothing except the reptilians disobeyed the council, which comes as no great surprise.

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:58.610
But you also claim that we've been misled by transdimensional aliens.

00:13:59.620 --> 00:13:59.960
Where is your...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:14.220
evidence of that there's a micro fracture in the magnesium jacket that's why it ruptured

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:19.740
i ran a pressure test tell it to the man lying in sick bay test them again all of them hi sir

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:26.720
commander i'm a little busy doc so it seems i understand you haven't slept since the attack

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.480
paul tadlin on me now

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:34.000
worried about you well i appreciate that but i'm trying to hold this ship together with spit and

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:39.200
bailing wire has it occurred to you that we'll be far worse off if you collapse from exhaustion

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:48.280
your concern is duly noted doc but i gotta get back to work i don't believe so come again i'm

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:53.120
relieving you of duty we'll go to your quarters and not return to your post before oh 500 tomorrow

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:59.460
six hours please don't make me involve security archer to dr flocks

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:03.150
Yes, Captain.

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:04.480
I need you in sickbay.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:05.840
I'll be right there.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:08.960
Well, Commander?

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:11.150
I could give you two hours.

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:12.950
I believe the number was six.

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:17.180
If I'm gone longer than three, there may not be a ship here when I get back.

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:20.340
Four. Not a minute, Les.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:27.280
Remind me never to buy a car from you.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:32.850
Captain's waiting for you.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:33.780
Where?

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:40.450
Then.

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:58.540
Him adrift.

00:15:59.710 --> 00:15:59.970
You reckon?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:00.760
denies his species.

00:16:01.756 --> 00:16:02.716
We've met one of them.

00:16:04.348 --> 00:16:05.348
What caused his death?

00:16:05.916 --> 00:16:07.616
Some kind of cellular degeneration.

00:16:08.124 --> 00:16:09.764
It started the moment he was taken off his ship.

00:16:10.012 --> 00:16:11.832
Perhaps your atmosphere was toxic to him.

00:16:12.028 --> 00:16:14.028
I believe our universe was toxic to him.

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:17.900
species evolved in a different dimension.

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.880
Under a different set of physical laws, he simply couldn't exist here.

00:16:21.308 --> 00:16:22.908
That's why his species built the spheres.

00:16:24.508 --> 00:16:27.128
to make our space more compatible for themselves.

00:16:28.092 --> 00:16:29.932
if he was a test subject sent here to see

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:30.720
they were succeeding.

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:35.180
And if they are, you're saying the Expanse will no longer be compatible for us.

00:16:37.548 --> 00:16:38.548
or any of us.

00:16:41.196 --> 00:16:43.436
We're destined to form an alliance to stop them.

00:16:44.588 --> 00:16:46.128
But if you destroy Earth, that'll never happen.

00:16:47.404 --> 00:16:49.364
You'll be condemning your own race to extinction.

00:17:50.092 --> 00:17:51.012
Trouble sleeping, sir?

00:17:56.844 --> 00:17:57.844
We were killed.

00:17:59.436 --> 00:17:59.976
This whole section.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:00.640
decompressed.

00:18:02.876 --> 00:18:04.256
Did you find a sealed compartment?

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:06.000
No.

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:13.380
You're dead.

00:18:19.036 --> 00:18:19.296
glitter.

00:18:20.028 --> 00:18:21.028
How's it going?

00:18:22.332 --> 00:18:23.012
I got as far as.

00:18:26.268 --> 00:18:27.108
to inform you.

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:29.220
That's a little dry, sir.

00:18:30.924 --> 00:18:31.684
You're not real.

00:18:33.324 --> 00:18:33.824
You don't have to.

00:18:34.124 --> 00:18:36.124
Sir

00:18:36.268 --> 00:18:37.108
So what's the problem?

00:18:38.124 --> 00:18:40.464
The letter doesn't have to be long, the captain told you that.

00:18:46.316 --> 00:18:47.256
can't think of anything.

00:18:47.884 --> 00:18:48.844
Wish it was that simple.

00:18:51.052 --> 00:18:53.172
I served on Enterprise for three years.

00:18:54.092 --> 00:18:56.472
You pulled me off to Saratoga to be on your team.

00:18:57.932 --> 00:18:59.712
Captain Brody was pretty angry at you.

00:19:00.508 --> 00:19:01.388
I forgot about that.

00:19:02.044 --> 00:19:04.884
You told me I'd make a fine chief engineer someday.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:06.080
You will.

00:19:11.644 --> 00:19:13.204
than tell my parents that.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:20.640
Tell them about the practical jokes Rostov used to play on me or that one time I found that glitch in the ejector assembly that everyone else missed.

00:19:22.108 --> 00:19:23.648
Tell them how hard I worked.

00:19:24.732 --> 00:19:26.472
Tell them how much you liked me.

00:19:28.828 --> 00:19:29.548
Can't you look at me?

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:36.160
Just...

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:37.900
And then...

00:19:40.524 --> 00:19:42.524
Is that asking so much?

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:43.340
Yes.

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:07.360
These tests only confirm the equipment belonged to the reptilians.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:10.830
There's also evidence of chronometric distortion, time travel.

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:12.690
The readings could have been fabricated.

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:14.450
You're determined not to trust him.

00:20:14.550 --> 00:20:17.610
No more than you seem to be determined to believe whatever he says.

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:20.820
Now, I admit, Archer's evidence is intriguing.

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:23.140
We barely know this human.

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:26.580
Our contact from the future has helped us many times.

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:29.010
She brought this council together.

00:20:29.190 --> 00:20:29.970
And you never want to...

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.080
and whether she might have an agenda of her own.

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:33.620
I am not a fool, Daegra.

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:37.110
All I'm saying is that it'll take a little more

00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:38.950
than a few pronometric distortions

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:40.490
to turn the council against her.

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:44.980
Archer is expecting me.

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:46.270
More evidence.

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:50.020
He claims to know a great deal about the spheres.

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:56.990
Daegra, I know you've had doubts about building the weapon.

00:20:58.220 --> 00:20:59.680
Don't let them cloud your judgment.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:09.180
We've been working to reconstruct our database.

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:11.850
Pounding your ships, Davis, didn't help much.

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:14.000
Try now.

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:20.720
Reset the optical sub-processors, and I might clear it up.

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:25.480
Let me slip through your detection grid.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:27.760
We gotta look at the weapon you're building.

00:21:29.630 --> 00:21:29.970
Press...

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:37.360
piece of engineering. Hell, it'd take at least a thousand starships like Enterprise to blow up an

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:42.270
entire planet. You know, I'd like to see the telemetry from the probe you launched against

00:21:42.270 --> 00:21:55.800
Earth. Increase the data resolution. Assume you were watching the attack. Calculating the blast yields.

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:08.400
damn excited. I mean, that beam cut one hell of a swath through Florida. That's the name of one of

00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:17.000
the places you destroyed. Florida. Did you actually see the cities burning? Houses? People

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:29.880
being vaporized? I had a sister there. Commander! There's Kelly. Just need a few more minutes.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:51.470
why don't you join me in my ready room until there let's take to the job at hand

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:53.600
bye sir

00:23:02.910 --> 00:23:05.170
The captain is trying to gain Degris trust.

00:23:27.910 --> 00:23:28.850
Plasma conduits.

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:31.430
when our sensors were offline.

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:33.260
Perhaps my crew could help.

00:23:33.560 --> 00:23:34.280
We'll handle it.

00:23:35.120 --> 00:23:36.880
We'll need to shut down the main plasma feet.

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:38.260
The flow regulators are damaged.

00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:40.650
There are manual cutoffs here and here,

00:23:40.710 --> 00:23:42.110
but we can only access it from outside.

00:23:42.390 --> 00:23:43.650
That's very close to the fire.

00:23:44.280 --> 00:23:46.280
My choice.

00:23:46.990 --> 00:23:48.090
If we don't get control of it fast,

00:23:48.230 --> 00:23:49.090
it'll spread to the reactor.

00:23:49.820 --> 00:23:50.280
Get going.

00:23:50.520 --> 00:23:51.460
I could use a hand.

00:23:52.090 --> 00:23:52.710
That'd be me, sir.

00:24:34.190 --> 00:24:36.910
Open that panel, talk you through the cutoff sequence.

00:24:37.730 --> 00:24:39.670
Where's the other valve over there?

00:25:21.660 --> 00:25:21.840
I'm done.

00:25:31.500 --> 00:25:34.150
Use your plasma torch. I'll be there in a minute.

00:25:35.100 --> 00:25:36.960
Releasing the interlocks on the first port.

00:25:48.580 --> 00:25:52.790
There you go, high-pass relays, Malcolm.

00:25:54.360 --> 00:25:55.700
Manifold pressure is increasing.

00:25:56.140 --> 00:25:59.280
We have less than six minutes before the fire reaches the reactor shielding.

00:26:01.500 --> 00:26:02.160
Barcher to trip.

00:26:02.380 --> 00:26:04.020
You've had less than six minutes.

00:26:04.560 --> 00:26:05.040
Understood.

00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:21.400
Dean, return lieutenant Reed's suit is over 44 degrees.

00:26:22.040 --> 00:26:23.220
He's too close to the fire.

00:26:23.360 --> 00:26:24.740
His EV suit can't compensate.

00:26:25.080 --> 00:26:26.780
Malcolm, get back to the airlock.

00:26:32.080 --> 00:26:32.780
It's finished, Captain.

00:26:33.180 --> 00:26:33.840
That's an order.

00:26:34.060 --> 00:26:35.540
Get inside, Malcolm.

00:26:35.720 --> 00:26:36.600
I can wrap it up.

00:27:03.870 --> 00:27:04.550
36 degrees.

00:27:05.170 --> 00:27:05.630
Malcolm.

00:27:06.220 --> 00:27:06.940
I'm sorry sir.

00:27:08.250 --> 00:27:09.190
You're breaking up.

00:27:16.390 --> 00:27:16.670
Open.

00:27:29.110 --> 00:27:29.530
It's closed.

00:27:35.440 --> 00:27:35.820
99

00:28:01.080 --> 00:28:03.190
Tucker to Dr. Phlox. Meet us in the airlock.

00:28:08.220 --> 00:28:10.440
We need to bring his body temperature down. Let's get him to sick bay.

00:28:10.910 --> 00:28:23.600
Yeah. I hope he'll be alright.

00:28:27.890 --> 00:28:29.130
It's one more dead human to you.

00:28:29.740 --> 00:28:29.900
Trip.

00:28:30.510 --> 00:28:33.850
You had no problem killing seven million of us, but seven million and one is more than you can stomach.

00:28:33.950 --> 00:28:34.570
That's enough.

00:28:34.890 --> 00:28:36.110
I guess even Cindy have their limits.

00:28:36.170 --> 00:28:36.950
I said that's enough.

00:28:39.280 --> 00:28:39.600
Yes, sir.

00:28:57.620 --> 00:28:59.880
We've determined there are 59 of them.

00:29:00.700 --> 00:29:02.340
78 at our last count.

00:29:03.790 --> 00:29:04.150
78?

00:29:05.270 --> 00:29:07.170
We've had more time to study them than you have.

00:29:18.830 --> 00:29:19.610
I apologize for Mr. Tucker.

00:29:25.240 --> 00:29:29.980
I never expected to meet anyone who suffered because of...

00:29:31.020 --> 00:29:34.990
I thought the attack was necessary to save my people.

00:29:36.460 --> 00:29:39.780
I know. Believe it or not, we've had this conversation before.

00:29:42.230 --> 00:29:46.660
That's right. Our escape from prison together.

00:29:50.150 --> 00:29:52.930
The reptilians are correct about one thing, Captain.

00:29:54.100 --> 00:29:56.500
You have an impressive facility for deception.

00:30:00.120 --> 00:30:03.420
Erasing your memory probably wasn't the best way to earn your trust.

00:30:04.630 --> 00:30:05.330
Probably not.

00:30:07.950 --> 00:30:11.000
They are all connected by a subspace energy grid.

00:30:11.080 --> 00:30:13.980
Unfortunately, our data on the spheres' interiors is extremely limited.

00:30:16.240 --> 00:30:16.900
Maybe I can help.

00:30:28.720 --> 00:30:29.520
Did you get this?

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:35.270
first fear we came across was damaged. There was a breach in the outer shell. We've never been able

00:30:35.270 --> 00:30:43.890
to gain access to one. These scans are remarkably detailed for a military vessel. Enterprise was

00:30:43.890 --> 00:30:58.300
designed to be a ship of exploration. If we're successful, it will be a gun. Computer, begin recording.

00:31:01.560 --> 00:31:07.620
Dear Mr. and Mrs. Taylor, I regret to inform you that your daughter was killed in the line of duty.

00:31:11.120 --> 00:31:16.440
She was a fine engineer, and she died performing her duties.

00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:22.720
Computer, stop recording. Delete that.

00:31:34.160 --> 00:31:34.880
Computer, start again.

00:31:38.710 --> 00:31:39.910
Dear Mr. and Mrs. Taylor,

00:31:41.770 --> 00:31:42.990
as Jane's commanding officer,

00:31:43.190 --> 00:31:47.400
it's with deepest regret that I inform you of her death.

00:31:50.580 --> 00:31:55.380
She was a diligent engineer, very hard-working.

00:31:55.910 --> 00:31:57.720
Medical alert. All hands to stations.

00:32:00.540 --> 00:32:10.540
report we've detected a ship they've just passed through the cloaking barrier on screen tillions

00:32:10.540 --> 00:32:29.810
anyone else we masked a warp trail i don't know how they found this chris degra he's involved

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:35.540
sensitive negotiations with the humans I suppose the council authorized these

00:32:35.540 --> 00:32:39.970
negotiations no one authorized the development of a bioweapon but that

00:32:39.970 --> 00:32:43.630
didn't deter your colleagues from creating one undock from the human

00:32:43.630 --> 00:32:53.400
vessel immediately to seize the human vessel destroy both our ships if we don't comply

00:32:53.400 --> 00:32:54.200
stand by

00:32:54.220 --> 00:32:56.720
I said stand by

00:33:01.760 --> 00:33:03.180
We don't stand a chance against them.

00:33:03.820 --> 00:33:04.720
Not in the shape we're in.

00:33:10.700 --> 00:33:11.560
What weapons do you have?

00:33:12.120 --> 00:33:14.920
You expect me to attack a reptilian warship?

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:19.820
If we work together, we might be able to disable the charging weapons.

00:33:20.020 --> 00:33:25.310
Are you familiar with the design of that ship?

00:33:28.210 --> 00:33:29.740
Warcraft system.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:33.620
Then you know where they're vulnerable, where to target our weapons.

00:33:34.280 --> 00:33:36.080
The ship is heavily armored.

00:33:36.320 --> 00:33:37.780
At least we'd stand a chance.

00:33:38.030 --> 00:33:39.370
Those reptilians are sending.

00:33:40.270 --> 00:33:42.970
You're asking me to attack my own people.

00:33:51.830 --> 00:33:53.050
Seed to our starboard dark.

00:33:54.010 --> 00:33:57.320
I want your word that my crew won't be punished.

00:33:57.620 --> 00:33:59.910
You'll all be dealt with as the council.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:00.940
He still sees fit.

00:34:06.210 --> 00:34:07.550
He's nearly reached the Reptilians.

00:34:16.340 --> 00:34:17.480
Got their shield generators.

00:34:18.500 --> 00:34:18.820
Fire!

00:34:30.220 --> 00:34:32.800
Evasive maneuvers. Keep firing. Target their weapons.

00:34:42.460 --> 00:34:44.520
Dagger was spot on. He knew exactly where to head them.

00:34:46.040 --> 00:34:47.000
Open a channel to Dagger.

00:34:47.760 --> 00:34:49.250
Sir, he's charging weapons.

00:34:55.930 --> 00:34:57.350
Reptilian ship has been destroyed.

00:34:58.260 --> 00:34:59.980
Captain, Dagger is hailing us.

00:35:05.980 --> 00:35:08.960
Contacted the council and exposed our alliance.

00:35:11.620 --> 00:35:12.620
I had no choice.

00:35:24.540 --> 00:35:26.200
Crewman Rostov said I'd find you here.

00:35:28.200 --> 00:35:29.360
Repair crews are starting tomorrow.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:30.960
Try and get him some power.

00:35:33.350 --> 00:35:34.910
These assemblies are all fused together.

00:35:35.230 --> 00:35:37.820
I've spent the last hour trying to isolate the damaged relays.

00:35:39.530 --> 00:35:40.670
You might find this useful.

00:35:43.310 --> 00:35:44.150
Portable power cell.

00:35:46.560 --> 00:35:47.800
You see of our new Zindi friends?

00:35:50.660 --> 00:35:54.470
Is there anything I can help you with?

00:35:55.400 --> 00:35:56.760
Not unless you can resurrect the dead.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:01.460
Taylor had a real knack for this kind of thing.

00:36:03.500 --> 00:36:05.140
But Taylor's not here, is she?

00:36:06.620 --> 00:36:07.880
And neither is Crewman Kamada,

00:36:09.390 --> 00:36:10.210
Rens and Marcel,

00:36:11.440 --> 00:36:12.240
or a dozen others.

00:36:12.870 --> 00:36:13.790
So forgive me

00:36:13.790 --> 00:36:16.240
if I don't want the damn power cells!

00:36:17.100 --> 00:36:20.200
We found Taylor over there,

00:36:21.100 --> 00:36:21.800
outside her quarters.

00:36:23.310 --> 00:36:24.670
She's probably trying to get to her station.

00:36:26.610 --> 00:36:27.610
She made it a few more meters.

00:36:27.830 --> 00:36:29.980
I wouldn't be trying to write this...

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:38.000
damn letter because every time i start i hear myself saying what a fine young woman she was

00:36:38.000 --> 00:36:49.240
how how smart and full of potential i realize i'm thinking about taylor at all

00:37:01.850 --> 00:37:05.330
I tried not to see her any differently than the other seven million.

00:37:08.020 --> 00:37:15.620
So I've spent the last nine months trying to pretend she was just another victim.

00:37:22.250 --> 00:37:23.420
She's my sister, Paul.

00:37:40.940 --> 00:37:42.160
I envy you, Vulcans.

00:37:42.380 --> 00:37:49.350
You think that the loss of a colleague or friend doesn't affect us?

00:37:50.690 --> 00:37:51.270
It does.

00:37:53.120 --> 00:37:58.390
But if we give in to those emotions, they overwhelm us.

00:38:03.100 --> 00:38:04.340
You're the ones to be envied.

00:38:05.420 --> 00:38:25.360
The evidence you've shown me, they'll have no choice but to take us seriously.

00:38:31.800 --> 00:38:33.480
I'm more concerned about the aquatics.

00:38:33.620 --> 00:38:35.590
They can be somewhat enigmatic.

00:38:35.710 --> 00:38:39.260
But if we can sway them, I have a majority on our side.

00:38:47.390 --> 00:38:49.010
These are the coordinates of the council chamber.

00:38:57.260 --> 00:38:58.460
They're a dozen light years away.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:00.900
It'll take us weeks to get there.

00:39:00.980 --> 00:39:03.040
There's a shorter route, a subspace corridor.

00:39:03.520 --> 00:39:06.000
It's located in a nebula less than half a light year from here.

00:39:07.000 --> 00:39:09.170
That will show your helmsman how to get through it.

00:39:10.140 --> 00:39:11.620
I'll meet you at the far end in three days.

00:39:12.720 --> 00:39:14.160
Will it be soon enough to stop the weapon?

00:39:16.740 --> 00:39:18.580
I'll do everything I can to delay it.

00:39:25.620 --> 00:39:27.440
Use caution when you enter the nebula.

00:39:28.540 --> 00:39:29.960
A hostile species is not...

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:31.760
to prey on ships that approach it.

00:39:33.320 --> 00:39:34.020
Thanks for the warning.

00:39:46.250 --> 00:39:47.150
See you in three days.

00:40:05.760 --> 00:40:06.720
Computer, begin recording.

00:40:11.630 --> 00:40:16.180
Mr. and Mrs. Taylor, by the time you get this,

00:40:17.820 --> 00:40:19.800
Starfleet will have already told you about Jane.

00:40:23.160 --> 00:40:24.760
Since I worked so closely with her,

00:40:27.470 --> 00:40:29.090
I wanted to add my personal condolences.

00:40:34.380 --> 00:40:37.000
I have to confess, I've been putting off writing this for a while.

00:40:39.570 --> 00:40:43.560
I convinced myself that my duty is on Enterprise to precedence.

00:40:48.160 --> 00:40:57.410
The truth is, I don't want to face the fact that someone's so young with so much promise.

00:41:01.630 --> 00:41:02.570
could just be gone.

00:41:06.910 --> 00:41:07.850
I'm facing it now.

00:41:12.000 --> 00:41:15.790
I find myself thinking how important she was to me.

00:41:20.040 --> 00:41:21.060
She was a great engineer.

00:41:24.260 --> 00:41:25.140
She was my friend.

00:41:29.330 --> 00:41:29.970
She won't be.
